=== REASONING ===
mount_point_decision:
  The new APICallLogMiddleware MUST be registered:
    - AFTER chimw.RequestID and chimw.RealIP                    (so the recorded
      log row carries the canonical request_id and the real client IP, not the
      proxy's address).
    - AFTER TracingMiddleware                                   (so the recorder
      runs inside the http.request span and any otel context propagation lives
      in the same span as our DB insert enqueue).
    - AFTER LoggerMiddleware                                    (so the existing
      structured zerolog line still fires first; both deferred readers observe
      the same final status because both wrap the ResponseWriter via
      chimw.NewWrapResponseWriter -- the OUTERMOST WrapResponseWriter wins for
      Status()/BytesWritten() observation, and chimw.NewWrapResponseWriter is
      idempotent on an already-wrapped writer).
  The new middleware MUST be registered BEFORE RecoveryMiddleware in the chain
  position only in the sense that the recovered-and-converted 500 response is
  visible to its deferred Status() read; given chi composes middleware top-to-
  bottom and defers run bottom-to-top, "AFTER LoggerMiddleware AND AFTER
  RecoveryMiddleware" means the recorder sits just below RecoveryMiddleware in
  the r.Use(...) sequence, so its defer fires INSIDE RecoveryMiddleware's recover
  (i.e. RecoveryMiddleware has already converted the panic to a 500 by the time
  our defer reads ww.Status()). Concretely:
      r.Use(chimw.RequestID)
      r.Use(chimw.RealIP)
      r.Use(TracingMiddleware)
      r.Use(LoggerMiddleware)
      r.Use(RecoveryMiddleware)
      r.Use(APICallLogMiddleware)         <-- NEW, mounted here
      r.Use(ErrorTrackingMiddleware(...))
      r.Use(PrometheusMiddleware)
      r.Use(chimw.Compress(5))
  This placement is a hard contract for Prompt 10's tests.

non_blocking_contract:
  The middleware MUST NOT short-circuit, slow, or fail the user request when the
  async writer queue is full or the writer is unavailable. On full queue / writer
  failure it MUST: drop the entry, increment a Prometheus counter
  (api_call_log_drops_total) and emit a single zerolog .Warn() with the reason.
  It MUST NOT: return an HTTP error, sleep waiting for queue capacity, panic, or
  block on a DB call from the request goroutine.

defer_required:
  The middleware's recorder MUST be invoked from a defer registered BEFORE
  next.ServeHTTP. This guarantees that when a downstream handler panics and
  RecoveryMiddleware converts it to status_code=500 via writeError, our defer
  still runs and records the request with status_code=500. A non-deferred
  recorder placed after next.ServeHTTP would be skipped on panic.

vehicle_id_column:
  The vehicle_id column on api_call_logs is intended for OUTBOUND adapter calls
  scoped to a specific vehicle (e.g., tesla-api per-vehicle commands). For
  INBOUND requests the middleware MUST set vehicle_id to NULL. Parsing
  /api/v1/vehicles/{vehicleID}/... out of r.URL.Path to back-populate vehicle_id
  is explicitly forbidden by this contract -- we do not want noisy or wrong
  attribution of system traffic to a single car.

shutdown_semantics:
  The async writer exposes a Shutdown(ctx) that closes the input channel,
  drains pending entries with a context deadline, and from then on Enqueue
  becomes a non-panicking no-op. After Shutdown the middleware MAY still be
  invoked (in-flight requests at server shutdown) and MUST NOT panic; it MUST
  silently drop and increment the drop counter. Prompt 10 must assert this.

