required_test_file: internal/api/api_log_middleware_test.go (new in Prompt 10)
required_helpers:
  - fakeAPILogStore: implements the writer port; thread-safe, captures every
    enqueued *models.APICallLog into a []*models.APICallLog with mutex; exposes
    Entries(), Reset(), and a configurable BlockEnqueue/AlwaysFull bool that
    causes Enqueue to return false (signaling the queue is full) so tests can
    exercise the drop path without time-based flake.
  - newTestRouterWithLogger(t, store): builds a chi router with the same global
    middleware stack (RequestID, RealIP, Tracing, Logger, Recovery,
    APICallLogMiddleware(store, opts), Compress) and mounts a tiny set of test
    handlers covering 200, panic, /healthz, /metrics, /api/v1/admin/api-logs,
    /api/v1/events, /api/v1/system/status, /api/v1/sse-token, and a body-echo
    POST /api/v1/vehicles handler so request/response body capture can be
    asserted.
  - withCaptureBodies(t, on bool): sets API_LOG_CAPTURE_BODIES via t.Setenv
    so opt.CaptureBodies reads the override, and asserts the env is restored.

required_test_matrix (Prompt 10 must implement EVERY item below; each test is
named so its failure points at exactly one contract clause):

  T01_HappyPath_GET_Vehicles_RecordsOneRow_ServiceTeslasyncApi
    GIVEN  a router with APICallLogMiddleware and body capture OFF
    WHEN   client sends GET /api/v1/vehicles which returns 200 OK with body "[]"
    THEN   exactly 1 entry is enqueued into fakeAPILogStore
    AND    entry.Service == "teslasync-api"
    AND    entry.HTTPMethod == "GET"
    AND    entry.Endpoint contains "/api/v1/vehicles"
    AND    entry.StatusCode == 200
    AND    entry.DurationMs > 0
    AND    entry.RequestBody is nil/empty (capture OFF)
    AND    entry.ResponseBody is nil/empty (capture OFF)
    AND    entry.VehicleID is nil (inbound never attributes a vehicle)
    AND    entry.RequestID == response header X-Request-ID

  T02_BodyCaptureOn_RecordsRequestAndResponseBodies
    GIVEN  API_LOG_CAPTURE_BODIES=true
    WHEN   client POSTs {"display_name":"Roadster"} to a JSON-echo endpoint
    THEN   entry.RequestBody decodes to the same JSON
    AND    entry.ResponseBody decodes to the echoed JSON
    AND    no header value (Authorization, Cookie) appears in either body

  T03_BodyCaptureOn_TruncatesAt10240Bytes_RequestAndResponse
    GIVEN  API_LOG_CAPTURE_BODIES=true and a 12 KB request body
    WHEN   handler responds with a 15 KB response body
    THEN   len(entry.RequestBody)  <= 10240   (10 KB hard cap)
    AND    len(entry.ResponseBody) <= 10240   (10 KB hard cap)
    AND    a "truncated=true" marker is set on the entry

  T04_SkippedPaths_NoRowsEnqueued
    For each path in the skip list, assert the store remains empty after a
    successful request. Paths to cover:
      - GET  /healthz
      - GET  /readyz
      - GET  /metrics
      - GET  /api/v1/admin/api-logs
      - GET  /api/v1/admin/api-logs/stats
      - GET  /api/v1/events
      - GET  /api/v1/sse-token
      - GET  /api/v1/system/status
    Assertion: store.Entries() length == 0 after each call (the writer was
    not even called, not just "called and dropped").

  T05_RedactsAuthorizationHeaderInStoredEndpointAndHeadersSnapshot
    GIVEN  request carries Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi
    AND    request carries Cookie: session=xyz
    AND    request URL is /api/v1/vehicles?api_key=SECRET&visible=ok
    THEN   entry.Endpoint contains api_key=REDACTED
    AND    entry.Endpoint contains visible=ok                (non-secret query
                                                              params are kept)
    AND    the stored header snapshot (if any) replaces Authorization and Cookie
           values with "REDACTED"
    AND    when body capture is ON for the same request, neither "abc.def.ghi"
           nor "xyz" nor "SECRET" appears anywhere in entry.RequestBody or
           entry.ResponseBody

  T06_RedactsBodyFieldsByCaseInsensitiveKey
    GIVEN  body capture ON and a JSON request body:
             {"username":"u","password":"p","api_token":"t","Note":"keep"}
    THEN   entry.RequestBody parses to a JSON object where:
             - password  == "REDACTED"
             - api_token == "REDACTED"
             - username  == "u"        (kept)
             - Note      == "keep"     (kept)
    AND    the same redaction is applied to nested objects and arrays of
           objects (recursive walk).

  T07_QueueFull_DropsEntry_RequestStillSucceeds
    GIVEN  fakeAPILogStore.AlwaysFull = true (Enqueue returns false / writer
           queue is full / writer.full simulated)
    WHEN   client GETs /api/v1/vehicles
    THEN   HTTP response is still 200 OK with the original body
    AND    response latency is within 10 ms of an unwrapped baseline
           (no synchronous DB call, no sleep)
    AND    the api_call_log_drops_total counter increments by exactly 1
    AND    a single zerolog Warn line is emitted (no Error, no Panic)
    AND    store.Entries() is empty (drop, do not retry)

  T08_HandlerPanic_StillRecordsRequest_StatusCode500
    GIVEN  a handler that panics with errors.New("boom") and Recovery is in
           place (recovery converts panic to status_code=500 via writeError)
    WHEN   client GETs /api/v1/test-panic
    THEN   client receives HTTP 500
    AND    exactly 1 entry is enqueued (the recorder runs in a defer)
    AND    entry.StatusCode == 500
    AND    entry.Endpoint contains "/api/v1/test-panic"
    AND    entry.DurationMs > 0
    Implementation contract: this test fails unless the recorder is invoked
    from a defer registered BEFORE next.ServeHTTP.

  T09_Shutdown_DrainsPendingEntries_LaterEnqueueDropped
    GIVEN  the writer holds 3 enqueued entries that have not yet been INSERTed
    WHEN   writer.Shutdown(ctx) is called with a 2s deadline
    THEN   all 3 pending entries are flushed to the underlying store (drain)
    AND    a subsequent middleware call enqueues a 4th entry that is silently
           dropped (no panic, drop counter increments, store unchanged)
    AND    Shutdown returns nil under the deadline

  T10_VehicleIDIsAlwaysNullForInboundEvenForVehicleScopedURL
    GIVEN  client GETs /api/v1/vehicles/42/state
    THEN   entry.VehicleID is nil
    AND    entry.Endpoint contains "/api/v1/vehicles/42/state"
    Implementation contract: the middleware MUST NOT scrape vehicleID out of
    the URL or chi route context to populate the vehicle_id column.

  T11_LatencyOverhead_BodyCaptureOff_NoMeasurableRegression
    Benchmark-style sanity test (not strict perf):
      - Run 200 requests through the wrapped router with body capture OFF.
      - Run 200 requests through an unwrapped baseline.
      - Assert the wrapped p95 latency is within +25% of baseline (loose, just
        proves we did not accidentally land a synchronous DB write on the
        request path).

  T12_ConcurrentRequests_NoRaceNoLostRows
    GIVEN  body capture OFF and a non-full writer queue
    WHEN   100 goroutines each issue a GET /api/v1/vehicles concurrently
    THEN   exactly 100 entries are enqueued (no rows lost)
    AND    `go test -race` passes (the recorder must not share unsynchronised
           state across goroutines).

  T13_PrometheusCounter_IncrementsOnDrop_NotOnSuccess
    Assert api_call_log_drops_total increments only on the drop path; on T01's
    happy path the counter MUST NOT change.

  T14_NonAPIv1Paths_StillRecorded_UnlessSkipped
    GIVEN  a request to "/" (the SPA index) served by the SPA file server
    THEN   the request IS recorded (service="teslasync-api") because the skip
           list is path-based, not prefix-based on /api/v1.
    Note: This documents the intended behavior. If operators want to also skip
    "/" they will tighten the list in a later phase.

  T15_RedactionAppliesBeforeEnqueue
    Implementation contract test: spy on the channel send and assert that
    the entry passed to Enqueue already has redacted fields (i.e. raw
    Authorization tokens never sit in the channel buffer even briefly).
    This is the privacy-hot-path assertion.

